  "verbalization": "Vitetrifolin D is shown to have targets that ultimately lead to NCI-H1792, through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Vitetrifolin D interacts with mitogen-activated protein kinase kinase kinase kinase 2, which is targeted by a complex compound with a complex structure, and this complex is also a target of NCI-H1792. Similarly, Vitetrifolin D is linked to ARO, which is targeted by another complex compound, and this compound also targets NCI-H1792. Additionally, Vitetrifolin D is associated with Proteasome subunit beta type-2, which is targeted by the same complex compound as the previous targets. These findings suggest that Vitetrifolin D may exert its effects through a common pathway involving the targeting of complex compounds that are themselves targets of NCI-H1792. The evidence supports a mechanism where Vitetrifolin D interacts with molecular targets that are part of a broader network of interactions leading to the activation or modulation of NCI-H1792.",
